      "blocks": {
        "question_3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long does the battery last?",
            "answer": "<p>About 1 hour per full charge (two sessions), and about 2 hours to charge. A USB cable and a wall adapter are included. A green light means it's on; the red light flashes 3 times when the battery is low.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_4": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Does it hurt or get hot?",
            "answer": "<p>No. Most people feel a gentle warmth at most. Stop and contact us if anything feels uncomfortable.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "When will I see results?",
            "answer": "<p>Red light therapy is a long-term routine, not an overnight fix. Most people use it consistently for several months before judging results, and results vary from person to person. That's why you get 30 days to try it risk-free.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_6": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is it OK if I'm sensitive to flashing light?",
            "answer": "<p>The 10Hz and 40Hz modes pulse. If you have epilepsy or are sensitive to flashing light, don't use the pulse modes, and check with your doctor first. The same goes if you're pregnant or have a medical condition.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_8": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What if it's not for me?",
            "answer": "<p>You have 30 days from delivery to try it. If you're not happy, email support@thedailyglowco.com for a full refund. See our <a href=\"/pages/return-policy\">Returns & Refunds</a> page for details.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
